(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "ADR-2608196300")
  (:adr/title "verify-kip-quorum exited 0 on an empty subject; it now refuses, and is registered")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-19")
  (:adr/tags "detectors evidence-floor kip quorum co-scientist")
  (:adr/body
  "## What was measured

Iteration 25 of the co-scientist loop. `scripts/verify-kip-quorum.cljs` was one of
the twelve verifiers ADR-2608196100 found with no runner and no twin. Running it
required a classpath nobody had written down; with the classpath its own header
names, it ran in 0.2s and **exited 0**, ending:

    no :final KIPs that require a quorum.
      That is the current state of the registry, not a verification of anything:
      nothing has been admitted, so nothing needed a quorum.

The prose was already correct and already said this was not a verification. It
said it **to a human**, and handed every machine a zero. This is the defect class
this loop has been hunting since ADR-2608136000 -- *a check that cannot fail
reports the same value as a check that measured and found nothing* -- with the
distinguishing detail that here the author had **seen it and written it down**,
and the exit code still said pass.

## What changed

1. **Exit 3, not 0**, when zero KIPs require a quorum: the `could-not-answer`
   code, neither pass nor fail.
2. **A `VERIFIED` evidence line** counting KIPs whose quorum was actually
   checked. The pre-existing `SCANNED` line counts KIPs *read* -- two numbers
   that differ exactly when the registry is full of drafts (read 2, verified 0).
   Keying the registry's evidence floor on `SCANNED` would have filed the vacuous
   run as clean; keying it on `VERIFIED` files it as `:inconclusive`.
3. **`FINDING<TAB>severity<TAB>key<TAB>detail` lines** for rejected KIPs. The tick
   parses nothing else; the existing `REJECT` lines are prose it ignores. Both are
   emitted -- the human log keeps saying which signatures were counted.
4. **Registered** in `manifest/orgs-detectors.edn` (6h, 2m timeout, `:writes :none`).

## Three directions, measured with the same script

    --kips <tampered>   one hex digit flipped in a signature
                        -> FINDING error quorum-not-met:kip-0001, exit 1
    --all               untampered -> VERIFIED 1, exit 0
    (registered form)   VERIFIED 0, exit 3

The workspace's own rule is that a gate is not landed until it has shown both
directions on the tree it will actually run against. The tampered fixture is a
copy of `orgs/kotoba-lang/kip/kips` under `--kips`, so the demonstration did not
touch the registry.

## Consequence to expect, so it is not read as a fault

**This detector will report INCONCLUSIVE until the first KIP goes `:final`.** That
is the true state of the KIP registry -- nothing has been admitted, so nothing
needed a quorum -- and it is the outcome the change was made to produce. An
always-green detector over an empty subject would have been worse than no
detector, because it would have been evidence of something.

## Why it is here and not a fleet gate

It reads two west checkouts: `orgs/kotoba-lang/kip` (the registry) and
`orgs/kotoba-lang/kagami` (`did:key` resolution). Fleet ships one repo's tree to
a node and neither would be present -- the same reason the other `orgs/`-reading
detectors live in this registry.

## Remaining, from the ADR-2608196200 census

Still unregistered orphans that read `orgs/`: `app-content-address` (needs
`content-address.core` on the classpath -- crashes without it, same shape of
problem as this one), `d1-kotobase-migration` (17s, real output, no SCANNED
protocol), `duplicate-registrations` (55s, 10 `gh` calls, exit 0 -- needs its own
reading before it is trusted), `kotoba-pages` (cannot be registered: Playwright's
browser is not installed, so it dies in 0s).
Also open: three verifiers with a twin under `scripts/fleet-ci/gates/`
(`capital-pools`, `kotobase-persistence-policy`, `source-nul-bytes`) where one of
the two copies has to be chosen, and `verify-artifact-path-policy`, which skips 26
of its 27 subjects and needs an evidence floor before it is worth gating.")))
